      "The awkward middle case is the child who reads happily in one narrow area — football annuals, one comic series — and nothing else. Rewarding reading in general here usually backfires, because the child is already intrinsically motivated and the chart lands as pressure to abandon what they like. Widening the diet is a books problem, not a motivation problem.",
      "## What to put on the chart, and what never to",
