      "## What composing costs, and why that is the point",
      "Reading a story asks a child to follow a structure someone else built. Writing one asks them to build it. That is a far heavier lift, and the weight is the entire benefit.",
      "Consider what a child has to hold in mind to produce three sentences of story. Who is this about. What do they want. What is stopping them. What happened last, so this follows from it. Which word says the thing. How that word is spelled, or near enough. Where the letters go on the line. Adults do this without noticing; for a six-year-old it is close to the limit of what working memory allows.",
