      "What it does not do is supply the intent. A catalogue of ten thousand titles browsed only by what is on the front page is a narrow shelf with a wide warehouse behind it. Someone still has to go looking, and the going looking is the part that cannot be automated. Recommendation systems are particularly bad at this by design: they optimise for what a child already liked, which is the exact opposite of a window.",
