      "Both need practising, and only one of them can be outsourced. A parent, a teacher or a recording can supply the decoding so the child can spend everything on comprehension — and comprehension is where vocabulary growth lives. Words are learned from context, and context is only available to a child who has enough attention spare to notice it.",
      "This is also why the two activities should not be collapsed into one. A book chosen for the child to read is chosen for fluency: comfortable, easy, plenty of it. A book chosen to be read to them is chosen for reach: harder, longer, better. Trying to make one book do both jobs usually produces a text that is too hard to enjoy and too easy to stretch anyone.",
      "## Keeping the ritual alive past the age it usually dies",
