      "What helps is different from what helps a struggling decoder. Explicit teaching of inference. Discussion of characters' motives rather than events. Non-fiction as a legitimate and often preferable route, since it makes fewer demands of social inference and frequently matches a strong interest. And patience with a narrow reading diet, since depth in one subject is a real strength rather than a problem to be widened.",
      "Predictability matters too. Knowing what a reading session will involve, how long it will last, and what will be asked at the end removes an anxiety load that otherwise competes with comprehension.",
