      "This is why it is genuinely a skill rather than an observation, and why the tasks matter. Blending is easier than segmenting. Initial sounds are easier than final ones, and final are easier than middle. Two-sound words are much easier than three, and consonant clusters — stop, blend, string — are considerably harder than they look, because the child has to hear two consonants where they experience one gesture.",
      "A child who can rhyme fluently and cannot segment is not being lazy. They are at the point in the sequence where the real difficulty starts.",
